<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugoslav June oil imports slump vs May.</title>
<headline>Yugoslav June oil imports slump vs May.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The  Yugoslav Federal Statistics Office reported the following energy statistics:</p>
<p> CRUDE OIL IMPORTS		 JUNE	   MAY	 JUNE '96</p>
<p> Tonnes			     129,370     209,778	93,685</p>
<p> Million dollars		    19	    29	    15</p>
<p>OIL PRODUCT IMPORTS</p>
<p> Tonnes				29,517	59,811	53,490</p>
<p> Million dollars		     8	    15	    13</p>
<p>NATURAL GAS IMPORTS</p>
<p> Tonnes				 --	  13,558	  397</p>
<p> Million dollars		    --	     2	    --</p>
<p>NOTES -- Cumulative January-June crude imports stood at 1.104 million tonnes and were worth $184.</p>
<p>Cumulative January-June oil derivatives imports stood at 277,589 tonnes and were worth $73 million.</p>
<p>Revised cumulative natural gas imports in the first six months stood at 529,730 tonnes and were worth $79 million.</p>
<p>Figures refer to the Federal Republic of Yugoslavia, comprising Serbia and Montenegro. -- Amra Kevic, Belgrade newsroom +381 11 311 4305</p>
